      "notes": "ArcGIS item e2910cc3a8f84549ab7f0f8e8f99817b 'OC Tax Parcels (Public)' = MapServer layer Enterprise/EnterpriseOpenParcelDataMapService/MapServer/1 'Tax Parcel Plus' (490,784 parcels; maxRecordCount 2000). The files are 14 pages (OBJECTID_12 order, geometry off) of the parcels whose Michigan class code is 2xx (commercial) or 3xx (industrial): 26,128 parcels. NAME1 and NAME2 (owner names) exist in the schema but are NULL on every row of the open layer (0 of 490,784), so this source has no owner names; POSTALADDRESS (the owner's mailing street line only) is filled. A separate Oakland layer 'OC Tax Parcel - Stacked 101' is under the Oakland County Enhanced Access Policy and GIS Data Policy and is not used. gisservices.oakgov.com serves no robots.txt (404). Unlike Wayne County (portal terms limit saved materials to personal, non-commercial use), Oakland's open-data terms expressly allow redistribution and reuse for any lawful purpose."
